  "query_preview": "/TUESDAY THROUGH SUNDAY/...\nIssued at 230 AM CDT Mon Sep 21 2026\n\nTuesday...More of the same as Monday(cloudy with temps in the 60s) \nas the upper low nearby fills and weakens. This may allow for the \nsctrd shower activity to wane as Tue afternoon and evening progress. \nA clear out and sfc wind decrease may allow for cool overnight low \ntemps in the 40s by Wed morning, and may have to keep some fog in \nmind especially valley and ground types.\n\nWednesday through Friday...Ensemble and upper jet trends suggest \nthat the local area to benefit from becoming under the influence of \nsome of the ridging of the blocked pattern aloft, which like the \nprevious shift mentioned, would lead to some fine fair weather fall \ndays with highs in the 60s to near 70 and overnight lows in the 50s \nand 40s. Will have to watch for some upper trof energy to try and \nundercut the ridging and shuttle some showers or way Thu or into \nFriday, but the latest ensembles suggest an omega ridge to get \npumped up along the MS RVR Valley from subsidence off developing \neast coast deep cyclone and erode precip as it tries to near the \narea from the west Thursday and especially on Friday.\n\nSaturday and Sunday...Getting into a more uncertain period, but the \nsame ensembles suggest another ridge-undercutting trof may finally \nbring in some shower chances to the area Sat into early Sunday. \nCurrently temps look seasonable for the weekend.",
